<div class="card" role="group" aria-label="Provenance legend">
  <p style="margin-top:0"><strong>Provenance legend.</strong> Every statement in a case carries one of four tags. Colour is never the only signal: each has a symbol and a text label.</p>
  <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;display:grid;gap:6px">
    <li><span class="prov V"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> V Verified</span> stated in a cited source (the source ID is shown beside it).</li>
    <li><span class="prov I"><span aria-hidden="true">◆</span> I Interpretation</span> reasoned from verified facts; the reasoning is ours, not the source's.</li>
    <li><span class="prov R"><span aria-hidden="true">◧</span> R Reconstructed</span> inferred to fill a gap and labelled as such. Used rarely; none in the current catalogue.</li>
    <li><span class="prov U"><span aria-hidden="true">?</span> U Unknown</span> not established from the sources. We say so rather than guess.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
